				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Synchronize Element submodules and normalize format script\n\nUpdate the `Element` submodule to include a diagnostic probe in `Sky` for Webview registration, addressing silent failures where `_resolvers` maps are populated but `resolve` callbacks never fire. The new probe validates internal state (`_resolvers` and `_awaitingRevival`) and emits structured logs to `Mountain` via IPC, enabling precise differentiation between registration failures and resolver isolation issues during extension hot-reloads.\n\nIn `Maintain/Format.sh`, normalize whitespace in the `shfmt` exclusion logic to match project readability standards. Additionally, reformat the `case` statement indentation and remove inconsistent spacing in the `Current` directory resolution to ensure the build tooling adheres to strict formatting conventions.\n\nThese changes enhance the debuggability of the editor's view lifecycle and maintain consistency in the project's maintenance scripts.",
			"SHA": "5c0ff7cff17f4294f0249ff751c57382f7cef01e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T11:30:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update ignore patterns and format script for generated code\n\nExclude newly standardized generated code directories (`**/gen/` and `**/gen/**`) from Prettier and Rust formatting rules in `.prettierignore` and `rustfmt.toml`. This aligns the ignore lists with the latest codegen outputs from the `Vine` and `Sky` pipelines.\n\nUpdate `Maintain/Format.sh` to explicitly exclude `gen` paths during shell script formatting (`shfmt`) and normalize whitespace in the case statement for better readability. The `.vscode/settings.json` exclusion is also synchronized to prevent IDE from indexing these transient build artifacts.\n\nEnsures the build pipeline consistently treats all generated code (from proto, channel, and effect bridges) as immutable during development, preventing accidental formatting of auto-generated files.",
			"SHA": "2676deecb68c05ddf1bf5a5b1e07eac87d76a28d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:43:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Element): Simplify Webview effect payload construction\n\nRefactor the JSON payload creation logic in `Mountain`'s `CreateEffectForRequest/Webview` module to remove redundant line breaks and align comment formatting. Ensure positional `args` are correctly mapped to named aliases (`viewId`, `viewType`, `title`) for `SkyBridge` consumption.\n\nThis update streamlines the code structure without altering functional behavior, maintaining strict IPC consistency and improving readability while preserving the required PascalCase naming and argument mapping strategies for editor UI effects.",
			"SHA": "87d7300257a6eee7e55b67e633a4ba68d9145196"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T10:41:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Restore debuggability and fix IPC payload shape\n\nSynchronize 11 Element submodules to reverse aggressive minification strategies and resolve a critical bug in the native backend. Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker restore full source map generation, revert single-character variable obfuscation, and reformat ESBuild configurations to strict PascalCase naming, ensuring production builds remain debuggable and maintainable.\n\nMountain corrects the `registerView` payload shape by including the required `viewId` key, restoring functionality for extension sidebars that were previously dropping host content due to schema mismatches. Maintain adds recursive JSON array deduplication to ensure build idempotency.\n\nThese changes prioritize developer tooling stability, correct silent failures in the IPC layer, and align the build artifacts with project readability standards while maintaining optimization for production releases.",
			"SHA": "16e66325c50780d70bd532478446b38d3b15154e"
		}
